---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const description = 'How deltoro.dev handles information: no analytics, no cookies, no trackers, and what happens when you send an inquiry.';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Privacy — ${site.name}`} description={description} noindex={false}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>The short version: no trackers.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This site does not use analytics, advertising pixels, or cookies. Fonts are served from this domain.
        The only information I receive is what you choose to send me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;border-top:0">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What is collected</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing automatically, by this site.</strong> There is no analytics script, no session recording,
        no advertising tag, and no cookie set by deltoro.dev. Fonts and images are self-hosted, so loading a page
        does not call a third-party font or image CDN.
      </p>
      <p>
        The hosting provider (currently GitHub Pages) may keep standard server logs that include IP addresses,
        user agents, and requested URLs for security and operational purposes. Those logs are controlled by the
        hosting provider, not by me, and are governed by their privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>When you send an inquiry</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the contact form, the details you enter — name, email, business name, service, budget, and message —
        are sent to me so I can reply. If the form is configured with a form-processing service, that provider
        processes the submission on my behalf; the current configuration is noted below. If no form service is
        configured, the form opens your own email application and nothing is transmitted by the website itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        I keep correspondence for as long as needed to handle the inquiry and any resulting engagement, and I do not
        sell or rent it. You can ask me to delete it at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>The security checkup</h2>
      <p>
        The checkup runs entirely in your browser. Your answers are not transmitted anywhere. If you choose
        "Email me the results", your email application opens with the results filled in, and nothing is sent until
        you send it yourself. The score is not stored.
      </p>

      <h2>Client work</h2>
      <p>
        For engagements, I work from accounts you control, with the least access needed to do the job. Working files
        are kept on an encrypted disk and deleted after handover unless you ask me to retain them. I am happy to sign
        your NDA and follow your data-handling policy. Specific retention terms are written into each engagement scope.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what information I hold about you, request a copy, or ask me to delete it by emailing
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. I will respond within a reasonable time and will not
        make you jump through a form to do it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date below changes with it. There is no mailing list to notify because there is
        no mailing list.
      </p>
      <p class="small">Last updated: October 2026. Current form processing: {site.formEndpoint ? 'external form service (Formspree-compatible)' : 'none — the form opens your email application'}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
